# Local runtime env for `wrangler dev` (Cloudflare Workers).
# Copy this file to `.dev.vars` and fill in values. `.dev.vars` is gitignored.
#
# Public values (also present in wrangler.jsonc "vars" for production):
SUPABASE_URL="https://qlzvngegsemrzmyxwykl.supabase.co"
SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY="your-anon-publishable-key"
#
# Secret — only needed if you start using the admin (service-role) Supabase client.
# In production set it with: wrangler secret put SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY
# SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY="your-service-role-key"
#
# Optional — for `npm run db:push` without interactive prompts:
# 1. Create a personal access token: https://supabase.com/dashboard/account/tokens
# 2. Database password: Project Settings → Database → Database password
# SUPABASE_ACCESS_TOKEN="sbp_..."
# SUPABASE_DB_PASSWORD="your-db-password"
#
# Google AI Studio — admin import vision + Beyond AI image turns
# In production: wrangler secret put GEMINI_API_KEY
# GEMINI_API_KEY="your-gemini-api-key"
#
# OpenRouter — Beyond AI chat (/api/ai). Required for Beyond AI to respond.
# In production: wrangler secret put OPENROUTER_API_KEY
# OPENROUTER_API_KEY="your-openrouter-api-key"
#
# Telegram admin bot (@mgs_uz_bot) — user control via /users, /user, /ban, etc.
# Generate a fresh token in @BotFather if one was ever shared in chat.
# In production: wrangler secret put TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN
# TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN="your-telegram-bot-token"
#
# Random string for webhook verification (Telegram setWebhook secret_token).
# In production: wrangler secret put TELEGRAM_WEBHOOK_SECRET
# TELEGRAM_WEBHOOK_SECRET="generate-a-long-random-string"
#
# Service role required for Telegram webhook DB access:
# SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY="your-service-role-key"
